-- title:
--   Inertia moves p-th roots of x when p∤ v(x)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $\overline{\mathbb Q}_p =$ `PadicAlgCl p` carry its valuation with values in $\mathbb R_{\ge 0}$; write $I$ for `(padicIntegers p).inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ_[p]`, the image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}_p \simeq_{\mathbb Q_p} \overline{\mathbb Q}_p$ of the inertia subgroup over $\mathbb Q_p$ of the valuation subring of that valuation, transported along the inclusion of the decomposition subgroup. Fix $n \in \mathbb N$ and families $u, \beta : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to \overline{\mathbb Q}_p$ such that each $u_i$ has $\|u_i\|_+ = 1$, each $u_i$ is fixed by every $\tau \in I$, and $\beta_i^{\,p} = u_i$ for all $i$. Let $x \in \mathbb Q_p$ be such that $p$ does not divide the integer $p$-adic valuation `Padic.valuation x`, and let $\gamma \in \overline{\mathbb Q}_p$ satisfy $\gamma^p = x$ (the image of $x$ under the structure map). Then there exists $\tau \in I$ which fixes every $\zeta \in \overline{\mathbb Q}_p$ with $\zeta^p = 1$, fixes every $\beta_i$, and satisfies $\tau\gamma \neq \gamma$.
--
--   This is the local assertion that for $p \nmid v_p(x)$ the Kummer class of $x$ is not "peu ramifié" in Serre's sense: the extension $\mathbb Q_p^{\mathrm{nr}}(\zeta_p, x^{1/p})$ is not contained in any extension generated by $p$-th roots of inertia-invariant units. It feeds the inertia analysis of $p$-division points of Frey curves, being cited by [`PadicAlgCl.exists_mem_unitRootInertia_apply_ne_of_not_dvd_valuation`](thm.html#PadicAlgCl.exists_mem_unitRootInertia_apply_ne_of_not_dvd_valuation) and by the two statements producing torsion points on Weierstrass curves whose inertia orbit is nontrivial when $p \nmid v_p$ of the relevant quantity.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_PadicAlgCl_exists_mem_inertiaSubgroupIn_apply_ne_of_forall_pow_eq_of_not_dvd_valuation.lean

